  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0},{10,20,30,\u2026,900}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{0,10,20,\u2026,900}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{10,30,50\u2026,890},{20,40,60,\u2026,900}}$ is not a partition because the element $0$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{0,10,20,\u2026,890}},{20,40,60,\u2026,900}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $20,40,60,\u2026,900,$ that appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- ${{10,30,50\u2026,890}},{0,20,40,60,\u2026,800}}$ is not a partition because the elements $820,840\u2026,900$ do not appear in any subsets.",
